        "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcuyLryx-tm/",
        "caption": "📌 SAVE THIS — How to Retry a Failed Test (Playwright)\n\n⚠️ Freeze on this and the interviewer knows you’ve never dealt with a flaky suite 👇\n\n✅ THE MECHANISM:\n✅ No custom analyzer to write — Playwright has retries built in.\n✅ One line in the config: retries: 2. Or on the command line: —retries=2. Any failing test auto re-runs up to that count.\n\n✅ THE SMART PART (free with Playwright):\n✅ Gate retries to CI only, not locally — locally you WANT a failure to fail so you catch it; on CI a genuine blip shouldn’t break the pipeline.\n✅ Playwright captures a trace on the first retry — a full replay of exactly what went wrong.\n✅ So you get the retry AND the evidence to fix the flakiness, instead of hiding it.\n\nThe rule:\nPlaywright retries are built in → set retries in the config → gate them to CI only → use the trace on retry to actually fix the flaky test.\n\n💬 If this helped, grab my Ultimate Interview Success Kit for SDETs — 14 files in one:\n✅ 300+ Interview Q&A with answer strategy\n✅ 100+ Coding Questions — code block, explanation, complexity, DSA & design patterns\n✅ 3 sets of 100% ATS-optimised resumes\n✅ 45-day learning calendar & roadmap\n✅ LinkedIn profile optimisation so you start getting interview calls\n✅ A fully functional explain-your-framework with end-to-end, real-time scenarios\n\nLike, follow, and comment anything and I’ll send you the link — at a flash-sale rate right now.\n▶️ Watching on YouTube? It’s in the pinned comment.\n\n— Sreenidhi Rajakrishnan | SDET Interview Prep\n\n#playwright #playwrightautomation #typescript #automationtesting #testautomation sdet qaengineer interviewprep softwaretesting flakytests qajobs endtoendtesting",
